01:28:38.122 --> 01:28:41.638
certainly there's, I think, a role for both tiers,

01:28:44.265 --> 01:28:48.090
the local municipalities being the ones approving the development

01:28:48.246 --> 01:28:51.924
knowing the timeframes within which the water is going to be

01:28:51.940 --> 01:28:55.217
required, but then the region being the one signing

01:28:55.233 --> 01:28:58.575
the agreements. So I think they both need to be

01:28:58.687 --> 01:29:02.607
on board and have that coordinated approach between

01:29:02.639 --> 01:29:06.028
the two. And I guess that will be part of

01:29:06.076 --> 01:29:09.867
the framework, the allocation framework that's

01:29:10.367 --> 01:29:13.963
going to be worked out. Here's the water supply that we're expecting. How do

01:29:14.463 --> 01:29:17.111
the local municipalities work on allocating that.

01:29:17.882 --> 01:29:21.591
Yeah, and that's why we're working hard to see if we can develop

01:29:22.091 --> 01:29:25.236
a common framework on that going forward. Great, thank you very much for coming in.

