01:34:20.654 --> 01:34:24.331
a year's time from now. So I think the small projects can go now under

01:34:24.831 --> 01:34:27.221
that principle for my clients.

01:34:28.280 --> 01:34:32.053
As the projects are larger and scale up, it all depends on what the planned

01:34:32.553 --> 01:34:36.115
forecasted capacity is. And then you have to start to distribute that allocation.

01:34:36.388 --> 01:34:40.642
And I think if you have the water information from the functional servicing reports,

01:34:41.188 --> 01:34:44.463
you can approve development up to that capacity

01:34:44.575 --> 01:34:48.027
and then stop it. And so I think that that would be

01:34:48.123 --> 01:34:51.735
a fair trade in terms of getting projects based off the known

01:34:51.799 --> 01:34:55.205
capacity. But just to open it all up for this,

01:34:55.334 --> 01:34:59.238
I think, would be problematic and high risk. Like the previous speaker said,

01:34:59.270 --> 01:35:02.130
that, that would be a difficult situation.

01:35:03.030 --> 01:35:05.312
Councillor Schantz. Thank you.

01:35:06.083 --> 01:35:10.196
I appreciate that. And I appreciate that, you know, a small project

01:35:10.696 --> 01:35:13.795
is not going to be a major strain on the system. But we

01:35:14.295 --> 01:35:18.166
have to look at everything that's in front of us. And so my question

01:35:18.230 --> 01:35:21.167
